(footprint "SW_MX_Kailh_Choc_V1V2_HotSwap_Hybrid_alt1_4.50u_Diode"
	(version 20241229)
	(generator "pcbnew")
	(generator_version "9.0")
	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Cherry MX style, Kailh Choc V1 (PG1350) and V2 (PG1353) low profile mechanical keyboard switch, hot-swap socket, single-sided mounting. Plate cut lines: User.1=15.60mm square (cosmetic cover, all switches), User.2=14.00mm square (MX / MX Low Profile / Gateron Low Profile), User.3=13.95mm square (Kailh Choc V2), User.4=13.80mm square (Kailh Choc V1). Keycap: 4.50u (courtyard 85.68x19.00mm). No stabilizer PCB features. Plate-mount MX stabilizers can be used. Series diode pads on back side: pad 3 = anode, pad 4 = cathode (cathode bar on B.SilkS, body outline on B.Fab, cathode points up). Combined hand-soldering land for SOD-123 / SOD-323 / MiniMELF (LL-34, LL4148): 2.0x1.4mm pads at +/-1.6mm axial offset. With the bundled SW_Key_Diode symbol pins 2 and 3 are stacked (one net), so the switch-diode series circuit is complete at schematic level; on the PCB route the short pad 2 - pad 3 track shown by the ratsnest, and wire the matrix to pads 1 and 4.")
	(tags "switch, low_profile, hot_swap, diode")
